      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mhs.mb.ca/docs//municipalities/carman.shtml"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the Boyne River, a tributary that winds through the Pembina Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carman%2C_Manitoba"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every July, the Carman Country Fair, one of Manitoba's oldest running fairs, draws visitors to the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carman%2C_Manitoba"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Carman hosts the annual Tempo Festival of the Arts each February and April, showcasing local vocal, instrumental, and dance talent.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carman%2C_Manitoba"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Carman railway station now houses the Golden Prairie Arts Council, a hub for local arts activities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
